00:27:14,740 --> 00:27:25,760
say, M1, we have that M1 has
to be bigger or equal to M.

260
00:27:25,760 --> 00:27:32,080
So a bounded set
has a least upper

261
00:27:32,080 --> 00:27:38,000
bound if there is an element
that is the smallest, so

262
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:39,450
to speak, of the upper bound.

263
00:27:42,760 --> 00:27:45,035
OK.

264
00:27:45,035 --> 00:27:53,360
And so now we are ready
to state what it means

265
00:27:53,360 --> 00:27:55,490
to be a complete ordered field.

266
00:28:03,960 --> 00:28:35,340
So a complete ordered
field is an ordered field

267
00:28:35,340 --> 00:28:53,150
so that any bounded subset
has a least upper bound.

268
00:29:03,010 --> 00:29:05,782
OK.

269
00:29:05,782 --> 00:29:08,610
So that's a complete
ordered field.

270
00:29:08,610 --> 00:29:11,610
And so we have the
